---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { FAMILY, MAINTAINER, SITE } from "../lib/site";
---

<Base
  title="About & independence"
  description="Who publishes Can’t Explain, how it sits next to the Ministry of Doubt and Election Tracker, and how it stays independent."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: "Home", href: "/" },
    { name: "About", href: "/about" },
  ]}
>
  <div class="wrap wrap-narrow section">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>A hall, not a campaign</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Can’t Explain collects low-evidence, high-emotion accusations, pins each one to an
      original source and a Git-timestamped file, and presents them with observational
      humour. The joke is the gap between the volume of the claim and the thinness of the
      evidence.
    </p>

    <h2 id="family">Same family</h2>
    <p>
      This site is the noisy sibling of a quieter rule. The
      <a href="https://ministryofdoubt.com">Ministry of Doubt</a> asks how you tell
      conspiracy from failure without becoming programmable. The
      <a href="https://electiontracker.au">Australian Election Tracker</a> records who is
      standing, with sources, as open data. Can’t Explain keeps the same evidence habit
      and applies it to the claims that arrive already shouting.
    </p>
    <ul>
      {
        FAMILY.map((f) => (
          <li>
            <a href={f.href} rel="noopener">
              {f.name}
            </a>
            — {f.line}
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
    <p>
      Longer argument belongs on
      <a href="https://ozeunleashed.substack.com">Oze Unleashed</a>. A card here is a
      claim, a URL, a file, and a caption — not an essay.
    </p>

    <h2 id="independence">Independence</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Not affiliated with, funded by, or directed by any political party, candidate,
        campaign, lobby group or newsroom.
      </li>
      <li>
        No party or target has a right of review before publication.
      </li>
      <li>
        Launch is Hanson-heavy because that is where the pattern is loud. The standard is
        the same for every figure.
      </li>
      <li>
        Editorial rules live in the repo:
        <a href="https://github.com/coldix/cantexplain/blob/main/docs/TONE-GUIDE.md">tone</a>,
        <a href="https://github.com/coldix/cantexplain/blob/main/docs/CONTENT-MODEL.md">fields</a>,
        <a href="/method">method</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="limits">What this is not</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Not a news site.</strong> No daily file. No live blog.</li>
      <li><strong>Not a how-to-vote.</strong> We do not score parties or tell you where to put a 1.</li>
      <li><strong>Not a comments section.</strong> Tips can come in; publication stays human.</li>
      <li><strong>Not complete.</strong> Absence from the hall is not a clean bill of health.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="author">Author</h2>
    <p>
      {MAINTAINER.name}. Physics, mathematics and IT background. Australian voice. Builds
      public evidence tools. Published by
      <a href={SITE.publisherUrl}>{SITE.publisher}</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href={MAINTAINER.x} rel="me noopener">{MAINTAINER.xHandle}</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>
      <a href={MAINTAINER.linkedin} rel="me noopener">LinkedIn</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>
      <a href={SITE.repo}>Repository</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
